---
title: Garlic Naan
serving: 7
yield: 7
image: https://cafedelites.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Garlic-Naan-Recipe-IMAGE-27.jpg
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uLt663PbRfM
time required: 2 hours
---

== Dough ==

Proof your yeast by adding @active dry yeast{2%tsp} to @sugar{1%tsp} and @water{2%tbsp}(warm) in a #small bowl{}.

Whisk yeast with a fork, then cover to let rest for ~{10%minutes}. The yeast should now be fluffy and bubbly.

In a #stand mixer{} with the dough hook attachment, mix @all-purpose flour{3%cups}, @plain yoghurt{1/3%cup}(whole milk preferred), @salt{1.5%tsp}, @olive oil{1/4%cup}, @water{2/3%cup}(warm), and the proofed yeast. 

Ensure the dough is elastic but doesn't stick to your hands. If it does, add @?all-purpose flour{2%tbsp} until the dough no longer sticks to your hands.

Move the rounded dough ball to a lightly oiled bowl. Cover and let rise for about ~{1%hour}, or until doubled in size.

Divide the dough into seven palm sized balls.

Oil a plate generously and place a dough ball on the plate. Slowly stretch out the dough, working from the inside out. When done, grease the top of your dough.

Heat #skillet very hot - it will probably be steaming or smoking. Add some @oil{}(sub ghee) and then add your naan. If your pan is hot enough bubbles will start to form in the naan.

Cook both sides of naan until golden brown.

== Garlic Butter ==

In a #small bowl{} mix @unsalted butter{1/4%cup}(melted), @garlic{2%tsp}(minced), @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @cilantro{1%tbsp}(chopped). Brush onto all sides of the cooked naan.